      "claim": "L3 oral-exposure records for related inhaled corticosteroid esters/acetals show pg/mL-level systemic exposure after mg oral doses: fluticasone propionate geometric mean Cmax ~24–34 pg/mL and AUC0-24 ~359–367 pg·h/mL after oral ODT dosing (C132, C133, C138, C145, C150, C160); beclomethasone dipropionate active-metabolite Cmax 12–126 pg/mL after 0.2–2 mg oral doses (C148, C152, C158, C159); budesonide oral suspension Cmax 914.8 pg/mL after 2 mg b.i.d. (C149). These very low exposures are consistent with extensive first-pass metabolism and low oral F for this structural class, although no IV comparator is provided in these cards.",
      "card_ids": ["C132","C133","C138","C145","C148","C149","C150","C152","C158","C159","C160"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Apparent high-F records in other contexts do not transfer: withaferin A rat values of 32–87% (C52, C54, C90) conflict with human poor and mouse 1.8% outcomes; ipratropium 30–32% (C21, C65, C86) conflicts with multiple human AUC/renal-excretion estimates of 2–3%; estradiol 30–40% (C80) conflicts with human absolute F ~3–5%; paclitaxel 47% recalculated (C36) conflicts with multiple <10% estimates.",
      "card_ids": ["C21","C36","C52","C54","C65","C80","C86","C90"]
    }
